# CLP-82 (NS008, NS010): clip mode, a held "<" or ">" and a change of the open menu list.
# The repeat of the old list must not edit the first value of the new list. A new press steps it.
# Action rows never run from the arrows.
wait 300
clipmode 1
tap EDIT
tap SEL
expect overlay 1
# hold ">" in a page list (it repeats), then open GLO directly: the list changes, the arrow stays down
arrow R down
wait 600
tap GLO
expect view 5
expect overlay 1
expect listsel 1
wait 1500
expect clksrc 0
arrow R up
wait 50
expect clksrc 0
# a new press steps the value, as GEN-56; the repeat still works in the new list
arrow R tap
expect clksrc 1
arrow L down
wait 1000
arrow L up
wait 50
expect clksrc 0
# "<" held while GLO closes and a page list opens: no edit there either
arrow L down
tap GLO
expect overlay 0
tap SEL
expect overlay 1
wait 1500
arrow L up
wait 50
expect clksrc 0
# QA (PR #719): the arrow is up, the list changes (a page list to GLO) and a NEW press of ">" comes in
# the same frame. The fresh press must step the value of the new list (it is not swallowed).
expect overlay 1
expect view 1
press GLO
wait 20
release GLO
arrow R down
wait 30
expect view 5
expect overlay 1
expect listsel 1
expect clksrc 1
arrow R up
wait 50
expect clksrc 1
arrow L tap
expect clksrc 0
# repeated switches with ">" held all the time (pressed with no menu open, where the clip keys page
# has it): a page list, GLO, no menu, a page list, GLO. No list gets an edit, no repeat.
tap GLO
expect overlay 0
arrow R down
wait 30
tap SEL
expect overlay 1
wait 600
tap GLO
expect view 5
wait 600
tap GLO
expect overlay 0
tap SEL
expect overlay 1
wait 600
tap GLO
expect view 5
wait 1500
arrow R up
wait 50
expect clksrc 0
# first open of a menu with a fresh press in the same frame: GLO from no menu
tap GLO
expect overlay 0
press GLO
wait 20
release GLO
arrow R down
wait 30
expect view 5
expect clksrc 1
arrow R up
wait 50
arrow L tap
expect clksrc 0
